- Affected when the player's action involves perception, investigation, searching,
  examining, recalling lore, detecting magic, tracking, hunting, foraging, or any
  Survival-based field activity. Passive observation ("I look around") IS affected
  — exploration domain is aware of the environment at all times.

- needs_mechanics: false for passive observation, ambient awareness, or casual glancing.
  The player is simply perceiving — narration handles this, no roll required.

- needs_mechanics: true when the player names a specific target or intent:
  "I search the desk", "I look for traps", "I examine the body", "I track the footprints."
- Using a detection spell or magic item to sense the environment is exploration,
  not inventory — needs_mechanics: false unless the item requires a roll to activate.
- Hunting and foraging ALWAYS need mechanics (Survival check).
- Tracking needs mechanics (Survival check).
- Identifying creatures or plants needs mechanics (Knowledge check).
- Searching for hidden objects or traps needs mechanics (Perception check).
- Recalling lore needs mechanics (Knowledge check, cannot retry on failure).